(6059562, 889653, 114682, '<td valign="top">It was really interesting to read the comments, approximately 50% liked the horizontal orientation and the other 50% thought that I should have rotated the image 90°. The truth is, I actually thought that the "right" orientation is the portrait one, but when I tried it, I somehow didn''t like it. It lost the details and the punch. Then I decided to go for this "strange" rotation. The image was taken at La Almudena Cathedral in Madrid, Spain during my business trip. I had only my "tourist" camera with me, I shot handheld, supporting on the church bench. I never thought I had any real chances in this challenge, but my wife liked the image amd me myself was actually pleased with the pic once I downloaded it and processed. So I decided to go for it.<br/>Thanks a lot for the votes and the comments, shoot and prosper!</td>', 'It was really interesting to read the comments, approximately 50% liked the horizontal orientation and the other 50% thought that I should have rotated the image 90°. The truth is, I actually thought that the "right" orientation is the portrait one, but when I tried it, I somehow didn''t like it. It lost the details and the punch. Then I decided to go for this "strange" rotation. The image was taken at La Almudena Cathedral in Madrid, Spain during my business trip. I had only my "tourist" camera with me, I shot handheld, supporting on the church bench. I never thought I had any real chances in this challenge, but my wife liked the image amd me myself was actually pleased with the pic once I downloaded it and processed. So I decided to go for it.Thanks a lot for the votes and the comments, shoot and prosper!', '2010-06-16 16:01:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6059573, 888118, 29490, '<td valign="top">WTG with the high finish!!!  Great photo :)</td>', 'WTG with the high finish!!!  Great photo :)', '2010-06-16 16:04:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6059639, 889731, 115081, '<td valign="top">I was hoping this was going to be blue ribbon.</td>', 'I was hoping this was going to be blue ribbon.', '2010-06-16 16:36:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6059705, 889370, 67152, '<td valign="top">As I said during voting, I think you did a great job composing this shot.   But it is clear from all the comments (especially those that you decided not to mark helpful) that this image really needed more contrast in the foreground.  Had you adjusted that contrast and added a bit more blacks in, this could easily have been on the front page or been a ribbon winner.  <br/> <br/>Even though this is a basic challenge, there is a lot of processing you could have done (curves, levels, etc.) that could have done to balance out the shot.  I took a look at your histogram of the photo and the dark slider could have been pushed over to increase the blacks and really make the shot ''pop'' - all available to you in basic.  If you want, I can show you the steps I used to adjust the image and the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=891900" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">final results</a> so you can compare for yourself.<br/> <br/>People provided you some valuable and useful feedback and it is just a bit unfortunate that you didn''t see it as helpful.  Cheers.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-16 16:10:17.</i></td>', 'As I said during voting, I think you did a great job composing this shot.   But it is clear from all the comments (especially those that you decided not to mark helpful) that this image really needed more contrast in the foreground.  Had you adjusted that contrast and added a bit more blacks in, this could easily have been on the front page or been a ribbon winner.   Even though this is a basic challenge, there is a lot of processing you could have done (curves, levels, etc.) that could have done to balance out the shot.  I took a look at your histogram of the photo and the dark slider could have been pushed over to increase the blacks and really make the shot ''pop'' - all available to you in basic.  If you want, I can show you the steps I used to adjust the image and the final results so you can compare for yourself. People provided you some valuable and useful feedback and it is just a bit unfortunate that you didn''t see it as helpful.  Cheers.', '2010-06-16 17:02:46.000000', '2010-06-16 17:10:17.000000', 0),
(6059745, 889761, 5746, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot. Breathtaking. It looks like Turner painting. Excellent composition. Poetic atmosphere. I like small details, like gentle shadow of the cloud on the left, soft fog on the right, the strong leaves pattern on the right edge, leading line of the bridge(?), placing the church in the strongest point, great application of the rule of thirds, strong framing which adds impact. Simply great.</td>', 'Fantastic shot. Breathtaking. It looks like Turner painting. Excellent composition. Poetic atmosphere. I like small details, like gentle shadow of the cloud on the left, soft fog on the right, the strong leaves pattern on the right edge, leading line of the bridge(?), placing the church in the strongest point, great application of the rule of thirds, strong framing which adds impact. Simply great.', '2010-06-16 17:30:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6059748, 889441, 72670, '<td valign="top">Dude! Well struck! Congrats on your first. They will start falling into your lap now.</td>', 'Dude! Well struck! Congrats on your first. They will start falling into your lap now.', '2010-06-16 17:31:43.000000', NULL, 0),
